erDiagram

%% The same order book, revealed a step at a time.
%% Both of this kind's timeline targets are named below: an entity — under
%% the name its author wrote, never the alias its box draws — and a
%% relationship, under the `${from}-${to}` id the model assigns it.
%% An attribute is not a target: its cells are drawn inside the entity's own
%% group, so the box that owns a row is what animates it.

CUSTOMER["Customer Account"] {
  string id PK
  string name
}

CUSTOMER ||--o{ ORDER : places
ORDER ||--|{ LINE-ITEM : contains

timeline:
  step 1: enter CUSTOMER fade
  step 2: enter ORDER slide-top, enter CUSTOMER-ORDER fade
  step 3: enter LINE-ITEM slide-right, enter ORDER-LINE-ITEM fade
  step 4: highlight CUSTOMER outline
  step 5: highlight CUSTOMER-ORDER glow, unhighlight CUSTOMER
  step 6: exit ORDER-LINE-ITEM fade, exit LINE-ITEM slide-right
